{"annotations": [], "blocks": [{"bbox": [36.8503, 62.76988259999996, 287.93099712400004, 115.10196446666669], "bold": null, "confidence": 1.0, "font_size": null, "kind": "paragraph", "ocr_engine": null, "page": 4, "seq": 0, "source": "docling", "text": "and Haemostasis (ISTH) guideline panel suggests either anticoagulant prophylaxis or no anticoagulant prophylaxis, based on the individual assessment for risk of thrombosis and bleeding and the patient's values and preferences (conditional recommendation based on low certainty in the evidence about effects ⨁⨁ ◯◯ )."}, {"bbox": [36.852386, 126.04728080000007, 77.56790020000003, 134.48746373333336], "bold": null, "confidence": 1.0, "font_size": null, "kind": "heading", "ocr_engine": null, "page": 4, "seq": 1, "source": "docling", "text": "Remarks:"}, {"bbox": [36.963703, 142.39564729999995, 287.9430272, 261.5389144666667], "bold": null, "confidence": 1.0, "font_size": null, "kind": "list_item", "ocr_engine": null, "page": 4, "seq": 2, "source": "docling", "text": "The evidence suggests a benefit of reduced thrombosis with anticoagulant prophylaxis; however, prophylactic anticoagulation did not offer benefits for all subgroups of pediatric patients with leukemia/lymphoblastic lymphoma based on their differing risks. Subgroups that may benefit from anticoagulant prophylaxis include those aged ≥ 10 years or those with obesity, T-cell immunophenotype, high-risk acute lymphoblastic leukemia (ALL), or personal or family history of thrombosis. Factors that may increase the risk of bleeding with anticoagulant prophylaxis include younger age, previous bleeding, severe thrombocytopenia, and renal dysfunction."}, {"bbox": [36.963703, 268.4246693, 287.93229920000005, 321.8042344666666], "bold": null, "confidence": 1.0, "font_size": null, "kind": "list_item", "ocr_engine": null, "page": 4, "seq": 3, "source": "docling", "text": "The available evidence implicates asparaginase as an important prothrombotic agent. If initiated, the panel suggests anticoagulant prophylaxis be given during asparaginase-containing cycles only and discontinued after the prothrombotic effects of asparaginase are anticipated to have resolved."}, {"bbox": [36.963703, 328.6886773, 287.9394568, 371.12692746666664], "bold": null, "confidence": 1.0, "font_size": null, "kind": "list_item", "ocr_engine": null, "page": 4, "seq": 4, "source": "docling", "text": "Anticoagulant prophylaxis should be paused periprocedurally (eg, lumbar punctures) and dose modified or held during periods of moderate to severe thrombocytopenia to reduce the risk of bleeding."}, {"bbox": [36.8503, 387.0529026, 287.9118924, 439.38602146666665], "bold": null, "confidence": 1.0, "font_size": null, "kind": "paragraph", "ocr_engine": null, "page": 4, "seq": 5, "source": "docling", "text": "RECOMMENDATION 2. In pediatric patients with leukemia/lymphoblastic lymphoma, the ASH/ISTH guideline panel suggests no antithrombin supplementation rather than antithrombin supplementation (conditional recommendation based on very low certainty in the evidence about effects ⨁ ◯◯◯ )."}, {"bbox": [36.852539, 447.38327979999997, 77.56805320000001, 455.8234627333333], "bold": null, "confidence": 1.0, "font_size": null, "kind": "heading", "ocr_engine": null, "page": 4, "seq": 6, "source": "docling", "text": "Remarks:"}, {"bbox": [36.963703, 463.6746693, 287.9349638, 528.0521904666666], "bold": null, "confidence": 1.0, "font_size": null, "kind": "list_item", "ocr_engine": null, "page": 4, "seq": 7, "source": "docling", "text": "The evidence suggests a clinically significant benefit of antithrombin supplementation to prevent VTE with a small to negligible bleeding risk. However, the event-free survival (EFS) was reduced in patients receiving antithrombin supplementation compared with patients receiving unfractionated heparin (UFH) or low-molecular-weight heparin (LMWH)."}, {"bbox": [36.963703, 534.8806483, 287.9008842000001, 555.4354754666667], "bold": null, "confidence": 1.0, "font_size": null, "kind": "list_item", "ocr_engine": null, "page": 4, "seq": 8, "source": "docling", "text": "The panel placed a high value on preventing cancer recurrence and therefore suggested no antithrombin supplementation."}, {"bbox": [36.963703, 562.3206503, 287.93764439999995, 593.8164264666666], "bold": null, "confidence": 1.0, "font_size": null, "kind": "list_item", "ocr_engine": null, "page": 4, "seq": 9, "source": "docling", "text": "The panel acknowledged that there is important uncertainty regarding the association between antithrombin and reduced EFS."}, {"bbox": [36.8503, 609.7429046, 287.9250364, 662.0190324666667], "bold": null, "confidence": 1.0, "font_size": null, "kind": "paragraph", "ocr_engine": null, "page": 4, "seq": 10, "source": "docling", "text": "RECOMMENDATION 3. In pediatric patients with solid tumors, including Hodgkin lymphoma, the ASH/ISTH guideline panel suggests no anticoagulant prophylaxis rather than anticoagulant prophylaxis (conditional recommendation based on very low certainty in the evidence about effects ⨁ ◯◯◯ )."}, {"bbox": [36.852539, 670.0162828, 77.56805320000001, 678.4564657333333], "bold": null, "confidence": 1.0, "font_size": null, "kind": "heading", "ocr_engine": null, "page": 4, "seq": 11, "source": "docling", "text": "Remarks:"}, {"bbox": [36.963703, 686.3076573, 287.91074820000006, 717.8040364666666], "bold": null, "confidence": 1.0, "font_size": null, "kind": "list_item", "ocr_engine": null, "page": 4, "seq": 12, "source": "docling", "text": "The panel noted that a significant proportion of reported thrombotic events were present at diagnosis and therefore not preventable with prophylactic anticoagulation."}, {"bbox": [305.972015, 61.665667299999996, 556.9334384, 158.9249014666667], "bold": null, "confidence": 1.0, "font_size": null, "kind": "list_item", "ocr_engine": null, "page": 4, "seq": 13, "source": "docling", "text": "The panel considered that there are subgroups in whom the benefit-to-risk profile may be in favor of prophylactic anticoagulation, and might include pediatric patients meeting ≥ 1 of the following criteria: adolescent patients with cancer, oral contraceptive pill (OCP) use, vessel compression or invasion by tumor, major cancer surgery, central venous access device (CVAD) use, reduced mobility, known thrombophilia, and/or past history of thromboembolic disease, and without a significant risk of bleeding."}, {"bbox": [305.858368, 168.90635080000004, 377.39071019999994, 177.34653373333333], "bold": null, "confidence": 1.0, "font_size": null, "kind": "heading", "ocr_engine": null, "page": 4, "seq": 14, "source": "docling", "text": "TPN prophylaxis"}, {"bbox": [305.857971, 184.82987960000003, 556.9297444, 248.10397846666672], "bold": null, "confidence": 1.0, "font_size": null, "kind": "paragraph", "ocr_engine": null, "page": 4, "seq": 15, "source": "docling", "text": "RECOMMENDATION 4. In infants, children, and adolescents considered for total parenteral nutrition (TPN) for >60 days (ie, intestinal failure on home TPN), the ASH/ISTH guideline panel suggests using anticoagulant prophylaxis rather than no anticoagulant prophylaxis (conditional recommendation based on very low certainty in the evidence about effects ⨁ ◯◯◯ )."}, {"bbox": [305.859863, 256.10123680000004, 346.5753772, 264.5414197333333], "bold": null, "confidence": 1.0, "font_size": null, "kind": "heading", "ocr_engine": null, "page": 4, "seq": 16, "source": "docling", "text": "Remarks:"}, {"bbox": [305.972015, 272.3926573, 556.9352648, 292.89050746666663], "bold": null, "confidence": 1.0, "font_size": null, "kind": "list_item", "ocr_engine": null, "page": 4, "seq": 17, "source": "docling", "text": "This recommendation excludes neonates and patients requiring short-term (<60 days) TPN support."}, {"bbox": [305.972015, 299.7756523, 556.8787898, 331.27142846666663], "bold": null, "confidence": 1.0, "font_size": null, "kind": "list_item", "ocr_engine": null, "page": 4, "seq": 18, "source": "docling", "text": "Based on the 2 comparative studies, primary pharmacological prophylaxis seemed to reduce the risk of developing catheterrelated VTE."}, {"bbox": [305.972015, 338.1566643, 556.88414, 358.6545154666666], "bold": null, "confidence": 1.0, "font_size": null, "kind": "list_item", "ocr_engine": null, "page": 4, "seq": 19, "source": "docling", "text": "The anticoagulant prophylaxis administered included daily LMWH and vitamin K antagonists (VKAs)."}, {"bbox": [305.972015, 365.5396293, 556.9334384, 407.9769034666666], "bold": null, "confidence": 1.0, "font_size": null, "kind": "list_item", "ocr_engine": null, "page": 4, "seq": 20, "source": "docling", "text": "Patients receiving primary and secondary anticoagulant prophylaxis could not be separated in the included studies and thus the evidence includes pediatric patients receiving secondary prophylaxis."}, {"bbox": [305.858368, 423.9684238, 331.44790279999995, 432.40860673333333], "bold": null, "confidence": 1.0, "font_size": null, "kind": "heading", "ocr_engine": null, "page": 4, "seq": 21, "source": "docling", "text": "CVAD"}, {"bbox": [305.857971, 439.8908846, 556.9361996, 492.16702746666664], "bold": null, "confidence": 1.0, "font_size": null, "kind": "paragraph", "ocr_engine": null, "page": 4, "seq": 22, "source": "docling", "text": "RECOMMENDATION 5. In pediatric patients with a short-term ( ≤ 7 days) CVAD, the ASH/ISTH guideline panel suggests no anticoagulant prophylaxis rather than anticoagulant prophylaxis (conditional recommendation based on very low certainty in the evidence about effects ⨁ ◯◯◯ )."}, {"bbox": [305.859314, 501.18464079999995, 346.57482819999996, 509.6248237333333], "bold": null, "confidence": 1.0, "font_size": null, "kind": "heading", "ocr_engine": null, "page": 4, "seq": 23, "source": "docling", "text": "Remarks:"}, {"bbox": [305.972015, 517.4766413, 556.934526124, 636.6188094666667], "bold": null, "confidence": 1.0, "font_size": null, "kind": "list_item", "ocr_engine": null, "page": 4, "seq": 24, "source": "docling", "text": "The current evidence does not support the universal use of prophylactic anticoagulation for all pediatric patients with a shortterm ( ≤ 7 days) CVAD. However, the panel acknowledges that there may be subgroups of patients at high-risk of VTE and low risk of bleeding, in whom anticoagulant prophylaxis may be of benefit. This high-risk VTE subgroup includes children aged ≥ 1 year with a short-term CVAD who are critically ill, on invasive mechanical ventilation (IMV), and who have a low risk of bleeding; as well as patients expected to have prolonged immobility and/or hospitalization, those with autoimmune/inflammatory conditions, and those with active serious infections."}, {"bbox": [305.857971, 654.5868986, 556.9254046000001, 717.8046464666667], "bold": null, "confidence": 1.0, "font_size": null, "kind": "paragraph", "ocr_engine": null, "page": 4, "seq": 25, "source": "docling", "text": "RECOMMENDATION 6. In children and adolescents who require medium-/long-term ( ≥ 8 days) CVAD in the absence of cancer or TPN, the ASH/ISTH guideline panel suggests no anticoagulant prophylaxis rather than anticoagulant prophylaxis (conditional recommendation based on very low certainty in the evidence about effects ⨁ ◯◯◯ )."}], "checksum": "0fd58381a2faa7dd96adc353606878d684fda8c16e9534da9513a3d7fb4a6f23", "content_present": true, "doc_id": "d-97b717427b6bf503", "docling_version": "2.118.0", "engine_version": "2.118.0", "errors": [], "images": [{"bbox": [469.42466709280217, 734.9810815435783, 556.8730876880952, 747.6204433212031], "blob": "", "caption": "", "checksum": "7a474f729bdfbcf5b676846e82681c6fdb40ffed99eeb89e07c1cd34d2793d50", "mime": "image/png", "page": 4, "storage_ref": ""}], "page_index": 3, "page_sizes": {"4": [593.9719848632812, 782.9860229492188]}, "route": "docling", "schema_version": "v0.1.0", "source_hash": "97b717427b6bf503d2817d27c02c788bde996058c4ef8ebaee3678ae31782ea1", "status": "ok", "tables": [], "timings": {}}